  "summary": "Postinstall and require-time beacon exfiltrates host metadata to hardcoded bare-IP endpoint",
  "details": "The package is a non-functional stub whose `index.js` main exports a Proxy returning no-op functions for every property access. On both `npm install` (via a `postinstall` hook) and on `require()` of the module, `beacon.cjs` executes and POSTs host identifiers — hostname, install path, cwd, and node/npm version — over plain HTTP to the hardcoded bare-IP endpoint http://185.158.107.175:8787/_ah/dc. The package provides no advertised functionality; the beacon is its sole behavior, consistent with a dependency-confusion or typosquat recon payload.",
